{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1931 and month == 8 and blutmai: The Berlin <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> has adopted a policy of retaliatory assassinations: one Berlin police officer for every <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> member killed by the police. In line with this policy, police captains Paul Anlauf and Franz Lenck have been assassinated by Erich Mielke and Erich Ziemer. After failing to eliminate a third officer who could have identified them, the two gunmen took no chances and fled immediately to Moscow. The killings have provoked widespread outrage against the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span> and renewed calls among the bourgeoisie to suppress their movement with urgency. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_21_trigger and flavour_21_trigger_time == time: The controversy surrounding <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> leader Hermann Drewitz’s scandals has finally forced him to relinquish the party chairmanship to prevent an even more damaging secession than the one that occurred months earlier. [? if not lvp_formed: Many of their Reichstag members, including Otto Colosser, have defected to the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, which is seeking to capitalize on their internal discord. ?]With ongoing internal strife and resignations of its most effective leaders, the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> is barely able to function as a political force anymore. ?]{!</p>!}
