{!<p class="other">!}[? if lvp_merger_2_timer == 4 and not lvp_formed: The conciliatory relationships between the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, as well as previous occurrences of liberal cooperation, have led to a <span style="color: #FFCC00;">united liberal party</span> becoming a possibility. [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" or dvp_leader == "Dingeldey": The leadership of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> is likely to be the biggest stumbling block to a potential merger, however.?][? if ddp_leader == "Lemmer": The leadership of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> remains skeptical of further cooperation[? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" or dvp_leader == "Dingeldey":&nbsp;as well?].?] Official talks will be held over the next few months, to gauge enthusiasm and to create a policy platform agreed by both. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if bruning_event_timer = 3 and dvp_ideology != "Right" and not lvp_formed: Paul Moldenhauer, the Finance Minister in the Brüning cabinet and [? if dvp_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?][? if not dvp_exist: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?] member, has been facing heavy scrutiny following his proposal of a 3% levy on all government employees' salaries. The proposal sparked significant backlash from his party's business and civil servant wing, which the [? if dvp_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?][? if not dvp_exist: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> now?] relies on heavily for their electoral support. Despite this, he has followed Brüning's advice and disavowed the actions of his own party, creating considerable controversy. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if bruning_event_timer = 3 and dvp_ideology == "Right" and not lvp_formed: Paul Moldenhauer, the Finance Minister in the Brüning cabinet and [? if dvp_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?][? if not dvp_exist: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?] member, has resigned following his proposal of a 3% levy on all government employees' salaries. The proposal sparked significant backlash from his party's business and civil servant wing, which the [? if dvp_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?][? if not dvp_exist: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> now?] relies on heavily for their electoral support. This affair has considerably damaged their standing with government employees and cast doubts about their continued support for the Brüning government. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if bruning_event_timer = 3 and lvp_ideology != "Right" and lvp_formed: Paul Moldenhauer, the Finance Minister in the Brüning cabinet and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> member, has been facing heavy scrutiny following his proposal of a 3% levy on all government employees' salaries. The proposal sparked significant backlash from his party's business and civil servant wing, which the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> relies on for their electoral support. Despite this, he has followed Brüning's advice and disavowed the actions of his own party, creating considerable controversy. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if bruning_event_timer = 3 and lvp_ideology == "Right" and lvp_formed: Paul Moldenhauer, the Finance Minister in the Brüning cabinet and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> member, has resigned following his proposal of a 3% levy on all government employees' salaries. The proposal sparked significant backlash from his party's business and civil servant wing, which the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> relies on for their electoral support. This affair has considerably damaged their standing with government employees and will drive them towards the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 6: <span style="color: #B31942;">United</span> <span style="color: #0A3161;">States</span> President Herbert Hoover has signed the Smoot-Hawley Tariff Act into law, drastically increase their tariff rates and prompting retaliatory tariffs by other countries. It seems unlikely that this policy will help resolve the ongoing depression, and may only sink the world further in it. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 6 and not lvp_formed: In the Saxon Landtag, a considerable decline in support for the liberal parties is seen. [? if not lvp_formed and vnr_r_saxony >= 1.4: This election also marks the first appearance of the <span style="color: #D3D3A9;">**VNR**</span> on the ballot, securing [+ vnr_saxony_elections_vote +]% of the vote and attracting attention within the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>.?] The results has increased the desperation for liberal and bourgeois unity, as a solution to the decline in their vote share. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if lvp_merger_2_timer == 3 and not lvp_formed: Progress has been made towards a <span style="color: #FFCC00;">united liberal party</span>, the previously moribund 'Liberal Association' has been revived and funded by prominent industrialists, who view a united liberal party as necessary to combat <span style="color: #c00000;">socialism</span> and the surging <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span>. Furthermore, in the liberal stronghold of Baden-Württemberg, a merger between the two parties is already underway, even without formal approval from their national leadership. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_0_trigger and flavour_0_trigger_time == time: The fragmentation of the rural vote among several parties, a direct consequence of Hugenberg's leadership of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, has created an opening for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> to attract the support of this disaffected demographic. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if flavour_1_trigger and flavour_1_trigger_time == time: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> under Adolf Hitler have been gaining serious momentum in the run-up to the election, there is something about his charisma that attracts people of all classes, regardless of their previous political sympathies. It has become a debate within our party if they should be considered a serious threat rather than the bourgeois right. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if lvp_merger_2_timer == 2 and not lvp_formed: A <span style="color: #FFCC00;">united liberal party</span> is increasingly seeming likely, as negotiations between the moderates of both parties have produced surprisingly fruitful results. Despite this success, as always, the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and the left wing of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> have remained a massive obstacle to liberal unity. Leaders of both parties have called an emergency party congress to settle this disagreement once and for all, but the declining vote shares of both parties are a major factor swaying the rank and file towards unification, and it's unlikely the opinion of the minority will come out on top. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 8: The last <span style="color: #002654;">French</span> and <span style="color: #FFD500;">Belgian</span> troops in the Rhineland have been evacuated in accordance with the Young Plan. While this is a positive development for the Republic, conservative elites within the Reichswehr and Hindenburg's inner circle are now free from external restraints to replace our system of government with an <span style="color: #808080;">authoritarian</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">militarist</span> one.?]
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_7_trigger and flavour_7_trigger_time == time: Long-time and formerly influential <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**DDP**</span> labor leader Anton Erkelenz has defected to the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>! However, his limited influence within the party, along with the strong enthusiasm for the formation of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> by many on the left wing, has prevented a wider secession. Perhaps their shared hatred to plutocracy is what fuels their support for this merger? ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and (dvp_leader == "Scholz" or dvp_leader == "Dingeldey") and not liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed: Following Westarp's split from Hugenberg's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, [+ dvp_leader +] has taken a keen interest in fostering closer ties with him and his group of moderates. The calling of new elections has given [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz": Scholz?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz": the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?] another opportunity to negotiate bourgeois unity. However, this time, the effort is far more ambitious—an appeal for the consolidation of all state-supporting forces, rather than just the formation of a parliamentary group. While Westarp himself has little interest in merging with other parties, he is willing to participate due to conditional industrial funding, which is contingent on achieving bourgeois unity. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 2 and not liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed: [? if dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed: With Westarp's split from Hugenberg's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, [+ dvp_leader +] has taken a keen interest in fostering closer ties with him and his group of moderates.?] The success of the attempt to negotiate a bourgeois parliamentary group has gave momentum towards the bourgeois unity movement, and allowed access to more funds from major industrialists on the condition that the state-supporting forces must consolidate in some form. A new round of negotiations have been started by [+ dvp_leader +], calling for a joint electoral list of all bourgeois parties in the event of new elections. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed: Following Westarp's split from Hugenberg's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, [+ dvp_leader +] has shown interest towards cooperating with him and the moderate German right. The calling of new elections has given the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> another opportunity to negotiate bourgeois unity. However, this time, the effort is far more ambitious—an appeal for the consolidation of all state-supporting forces, rather than just the formation of a parliamentary group. While Westarp himself has little interest in merging with other parties, he is willing to participate due to conditional industrial funding, which is contingent on achieving bourgeois unity. The betrayal of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> still lingers in their minds, with many within the German right reluctant to cooperate with [+ dvp_leader +] in this endeavor. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 2 and liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed): Following the success of the liberals in consolidating their parliamentary groups, big businesses have increased pressure to either expand the parliamentary group to include other bourgeois parties or encourage the other parties on the bourgeois right to form their own separate parliamentary faction. Only the latter appears to be possible currently, with the hostility that has developed between the liberal parties and the conservative right. New negotiations have been initiated by Treviranus of the [? if (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed): <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?][? if not (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed): <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservative Association</span>?], featuring the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and not (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and (dvp_leader == "Scholz" or dvp_leader == "Dingeldey") and not liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed: The calling of new elections has given [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz": Scholz?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz": the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>?] another opportunity to negotiate bourgeois unity. However, this time, the effort is far more ambitious—an appeal for the consolidation of all state-supporting forces, rather than just the formation of a parliamentary group. The failure of the last negotiations has left a bad taste in the parties' mouths, with many within the German right reluctant to cooperate with [+ dvp_leader +] in this endeavor. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and not (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and liberal_parliament and not lvp_formed: The calling of new elections has given the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> another opportunity to negotiate bourgeois unity. However, this time, the effort is far more ambitious—an appeal for the consolidation of all state-supporting forces, rather than just the formation of a parliamentary group. The betrayal of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> still lingers in their minds, with many within the German right reluctant to cooperate with [+ dvp_leader +] in this endeavor. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and bourgeois_parliament and lvp_formed: Following Westarp's split from Hugenberg's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, there has been a major effort by major industrialists and politicians like Treviranus to lobby the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> to establish closer ties with the other right-wing parties. They have succeeded in this regard by convincing the party to be apart of the bourgeois parliamentary group, but has yet to convince the party to consider unification with other right-wing parties. The calling of new elections have sparked a new round of negotiations on this matter. The parties involved are the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and not bourgeois_parliament and lvp_formed: Following the failure of negotiations to create a bourgeois parliamentary group in support of Brüning, the calling of new elections have presented another opportunity to negotiate bourgeois unity. A major effort has been made by big businesses and industrialists to only fund parties that make an effort towards bourgeois unity, which once again has brought the reluctant <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> to the negotiating table with the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and csvd_formed and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**CSVD**</span>'s leadership has voted overwhelmingly in favor of entering the election with its own slate of candidates, explicitly rejecting any agreements with other parties for fear of compromising its identity. For the same reason, the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> have also dismissed [+ dvp_leader +]'s proposal for negotiations. [? if liberal_cooperation < 5 and not liberal_parliament: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has criticized the proposal as a premature initiative that lacked the necessary consensus on such fundamental issues.?][? if liberal_cooperation >= 5 or liberal_parliament: Furthermore, the closeness of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> with the more left-wing <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has alienated those on the moderate right. ?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 2 and bourgeois_negotiations_1930_done and not csvd_formed and dnvp_historical_1929 and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> have responded coldly to the consolidation of the vocational parties with the more ideologically oriented <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. It is up to people like Martin Schiele, a former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> member advocating for a party akin to the pre-Hugenberg <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> to persuade the reluctant old guard of the vocational parties. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_merger_trigger_scholz and not liberal_parliament:  In a great deal of surprise, [+ dvp_leader +] has managed to rally the bourgeois parties together, whether because a mutual fear of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialism</span>, past instances of cooperation, or stacks of cash offered by their wealthy donors; a shared electoral list is agreed upon by the majority of the bourgeois parties. The [? if kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>?][? if not kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?] and <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> candidates will be the dominant parties on the rural lists, while the more urban [? if kvp_formed or dnvp_split_2: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, ?] <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>[? if bourgeois_list_ddp:, <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will be the main parties on the ballot in urban areas. The national list seats are equitably distributed between the parties. This will severely impair the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>'s ability to appeal to the German middle. However, the right-wing tilt of the parties involved will likely make future cooperation near-impossible. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_merger_trigger_moderate and not liberal_parliament: In a great deal of surprise, [+ dvp_leader +] has managed to rally the bourgeois parties together, whether because a mutual fear of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialism</span>, past instances of cooperation, or stacks of cash offered by their wealthy donors; a shared electoral list is agreed upon by the majority of the bourgeois parties. The [? if kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>?][? if not kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?] and <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> candidates will be the dominant parties on the rural lists, while the more urban [? if kvp_formed or dnvp_split_2: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, ?] <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>[? if bourgeois_list_ddp:, <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will be the main parties on the ballot in urban areas. The national list seats are equitably distributed between the parties. This will severely impair the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>'s ability to appeal to the German middle. Despite the right-wing tilt of the parties involved, the somewhat friendly leadership of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will make future cooperation somewhat possible. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 1 and bourgeois_list: The momentum for bourgeois unity has culminated in an agreement for a shared electoral list supported by the majority of the bourgeois parties. The [? if kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>?][? if not kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?] and <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> candidates will be the dominant parties on the rural lists, while the more urban [? if kvp_formed or dnvp_split_2: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, ?]<span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>[? if bourgeois_list_ddp:, <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?] and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> will be the main parties on the ballot in urban areas. The national list seats are equitably distributed between the parties. This will severely impair the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>'s ability to appeal to the German middle. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 1 and bourgeois_list_fail: The movement for bourgeois unity has failed to achieve any meaningful goals this time around. The leadership of the vocational parties recoiled at the suggestion of a shared list between the plethora of bourgeois parties, as it would destroy their vocational identity. In spite of this defeat, some smaller agreements are able to be reached aiming to minimize interparty animosity. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 1 and bourgeois_parliament_no_liberals: The negotiations between the non-liberal bourgeois parties led by Treviranus of the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> have finally ended with an agreement for a parliamentary alliance featuring the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>. This is later joined by the <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span>, who, despite their objections, would be factionless in parliament otherwise. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_1930_aftermath_timer == 1 and bourgeois_negotiations_fail_parliament: As expected, the negotiations between the non-liberal bourgeois parties, led by the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, have ended without any conclusive agreements. The large number of parties on the moderate German right will allow the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> to capitalize on the fragmentation within the German middle.  ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_merger_kvp_trigger: In a great deal of surprise, [+ kvp_leader +] has managed to rally the bourgeois parties together, whether because a mutual fear of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialism</span>, past instances of cooperation, or the stacks of cash offered by their wealthy donors: [? if dnvp_split_2: The unification of the moderate German right-wing parties around the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> (<span style="color: #0087DC;">Conservative People's Party</span>) is currently underway.?][? if complete_dnvp_split: The addition of the moderate German right-wing parties around the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> (<span style="color: #0087DC;">Conservative People's Party</span>) is currently underway.?] [? if dnvp_split_2: During the various splits from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, the moderate wing has ended up in a variety of parties, owing to their background. Now, it seems that their urgency for reunion has overcome the desire to represent their special interests?][? if complete_dnvp_split: The leaderships of the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, previously opposed to compromising their own identities, have now recognized that the issue of bourgeois unification is a more urgent concern?]. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_parliament_trigger_5: Surprisingly, the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> have come to an agreement on the creation of a bourgeois parliamentary faction. They have published a joint declaration in support of Brüning and his policies, along with an electoral truce. The <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span>, however, is unhappy with the dominance of nobility and large landowners within the [? if not kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?][? if kvp_cnblp_sister: <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>?] and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. Despite their objections, they are forced to go along with the plan, as without a faction, they'll be powerless in parliament. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_negotiations_fail_elections and not liberal_parliament: The stubbornness of many within the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> have destroyed any chance of agreement between themselves and the rest of the bourgeois right. Despite this, negotiations between the parties [+ dvp_leader +] had invited continue, evoking cool responses from the other parties on [+ dvp_leader +]'s proposal for a united middle party. This has caused [+ dvp_leader +] to scale down his ambitions, and instead propose an electoral truce and a joint election appeal in favor of[? if chancellor == "Brüning":&nbsp;Brüning and?] President Hindenburg. Although accepted by all parties at first, opposition from the old guard in the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> has obstructed this proposal, but eventually, due to conditional industrial funding, the 'Hindenburg Program' is supported by only the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>[? if dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed:, <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?][? if not dnvp_split_2 and not kvp_formed: &nbsp;and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>?]. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_negotiations_fail_elections and liberal_parliament: The distrust arising from the formation of the liberal parliamentary group has effectively doomed the negotiations from the outset. The only outcome of these talks is a vague joint appeal in support of President Hindenburg and Chancellor Brüning's policies. A proposal for an electoral truce is rejected by the special interest parties, who instead focus on writing polemics against one another. While the disunity among the bourgeois parties might seem beneficial to us on the surface, the chaos and fragmentation in the German middle will give the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> a significant opportunity to capitalize on the situation. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_negotiations_fail_elections_dstp and not liberal_parliament: The formation of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and unsuccessful attempts to poach <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> members have left a sour taste in their mouths. Despite this, negotiations between the parties [+ dvp_leader +] had invited continue, evoking cool responses from the other parties on [+ dvp_leader +]'s proposal for a united middle party. This has caused [+ dvp_leader +] to scale down his ambitions, and instead propose an electoral truce and a joint election appeal in favor of[? if chancellor == "Brüning":&nbsp;Brüning and?] President Hindenburg. Although accepted by all parties at first, opposition from the old guard in the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> has obstructed this proposal, but eventually, due to conditional industrial funding, the 'Hindenburg Program' is supported by only the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>[? if dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed:, <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?][? if not dnvp_split_2 and not kvp_formed: and <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>?]. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_2_trigger and flavour_2_trigger_time == time: The state organizations of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> in Baden and Württemberg have agreed to run a unified slate of candidates in the upcoming Reichstag elections, without consulting their respective national leaderships. This has inspired a similar proposal in Schleswig-Holstein, but the national leaderships of both parties intervened, swiftly halting both current and future negotiations. This interference from the national headquarters has been strongly resented by the local party organizations, deepening the rift between the national leaders and the rank-and-file members over the question of bourgeois unity. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_3_trigger and flavour_3_trigger_time == time: The state organizations of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> in Baden and Württemberg have agreed to run a unified slate of candidates in the upcoming Reichstag elections, doing so without consulting their respective national leaderships. This move has inspired a similar proposal in Schleswig-Holstein, and soon enough, unified liberal lists have emerged across Germany. Although these agreements have not been officially approved by their national leaderships, they have not been blocked either. Major liberal leaders such as Hermann Dietrich and Julius Curtius have even placed each other at the head of a joint list in their own constituencies. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if bourgeois_negotiations_elections_1930_timer == 1 and bourgeois_negotiations_fail_elections_kvp: The negotiations for a united bourgeois parliamentary fraction to the right of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> but left of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> has failed. The <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, with their vocational identities, strongly objected to closer ties with the ideologically oriented <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. This has proved unacceptable to the industrialists, who once again coerced the parties into cooperation by making them sign a joint declaration on their support for Brüning and for an electoral truce. The disunity of the bourgeois parties and the resulting cuts in business donations will give rise to the extremist <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, who seek to capitalize on their division. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 1: Westarp and his group of <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> moderates have been finding their new home in the newly founded <span style="color: #0087DC;">Conservative People's Party</span> (<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>), <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>[? if stegerwald_path == 0:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**CSVD**</span>?]. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 1 and bourgeois_cooperation < 7: Martin Schiele, president of the National Rural League (RLB)[? if not spd_in_government and chancellor == "Brüning":, Minister of Agriculture,?] and the most influential figure in Germany's agricultural community, has been working to rebuild the connection between organized agriculture and the German right. This follows the rift caused by Hugenberg's actions that broke the historic bond between them and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. Schiele has proposed a plan to form a new agrarian party by merging the RLB with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, aiming for it to serve as a sister party to the <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span>, a party that would have greater appeal to urban areas. This proposal has been shot down by the old guard of the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, who are adamantly opposed to the reestablishment of agriculture to an ideologically oriented party. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 1 and bourgeois_cooperation >= 7: Martin Schiele, president of the National Rural League (RLB)[? if not spd_in_government and chancellor == "Brüning":, Minister of Agriculture,?] and the most influential figure in Germany's agricultural community, has been working to rebuild the connection between organized agriculture and the German right. This follows the rift caused by Hugenberg's actions that broke the historic bond between them and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. Schiele has proposed a plan to form a new agrarian party by merging the RLB with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, aiming for it to serve as a sister party to the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, a party that would have greater appeal to urban areas. Despite strong opposition from the party's old guard, Schiele, along with Günther Gereke—another <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> dissident with substantial influence—has managed to steer the party towards an agreement with the <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 2 and not kvp_cnblp_sister: Günther Gereke, a former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> member and a driving force in the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, has managed to persuade the party's old guard in going fourth with an electoral alliance with the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>. For his efforts, he has been handsomely rewarded by German businesses for his efforts towards bourgeois unity, which is how he managed to convince the wider party. If not for this, the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> will likely be without seats, with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>[? if stegerwald_path == 0:&nbsp;and <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**CSVD**</span>?] heavily narrowing the field for them to gain even a single seat. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 2 and kvp_cnblp_sister: The <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> has been disbanded, having been succeeded by the <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>, a unification of the National Rural League (RLB) and the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>. Regional affiliates of the RLB in states like Bavaria and Württemberg are prevalent enough to grant them double-digit supports in a couple of states. The <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> however, are unhappy with the preponderance of nobility and large landowners within the <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span>'s leadership, and will run on a separate list. Despite this, the sister party arrangement between the <span style="color: #385A38;">**Landbund**</span> and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> will enable the smaller <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> under Westarp to thrive, supported by funding from major industrialists who are pleased with their efforts toward promoting bourgeois unity. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if dnvp_split_2_timer == 2 and not kvp_cnblp_sister : The <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, having rejected Schiele's proposal, is now calling for the vocational solidarity of the agricultural community. This involves the RLB urging its regional affiliates to run on a shared agrarian list, uniting various regional conservative organizations with the aim of having them join the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>'s Reichstag delegation afterward. While this has earned them double-digit support in states like Bavaria and Württemberg, major organizations such as the Association of German Peasant Unions maintain their bipartisan neutrality. [? if not cnblp_dbp: The <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> are also unhappy with the preponderance of nobility and large landowners within the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>'s leadership, and will run on a separate list.?][? if cnblp_dbp: The <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span>, although dissatisfied with the dominance of nobility and large landowners in the leadership of the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, has chosen to run on a shared list with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> on the basis of vocational solidarity.?] ?]{!</p>!}
# not timer but dnvp split occurs anyway on the historical date of all the bourgeois negotiations so it will still work
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 8: The film adaptation of the controversial anti-war novel <i>All Quiet on the Western Front</i>has released in America, but has yet to arrive on our shores. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_8_trigger and flavour_8_trigger_time == time: Many youth and bourgeois unity organizations that initially supported the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> have since distanced themselves from the party due to a sharp rebuff from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s [+ dvp_leader +]. These <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> affiliated organizations, initially frustrated by the lack of progress toward bourgeois concentration, have now shifted their stance. They condemn the founding of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, arguing that it is incompatible with bourgeois unity, and called on the founders of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to join the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> in the creation of a truly comprehensive middle party. These events, coupled with the hostility that has arisen towards the party, have significantly dampened the initial enthusiasm surrounding its founding. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_9_trigger and flavour_9_trigger_time == time: The anti-Semitism and romanticism of the Young German Order have caused intense conflict with the <span style="color: #005EB8;">Jews</span> and old-line <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democrats</span> within the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>. A notable example is Gustav Stolper, a <span style="color: #005EB8;">Jew</span> who faced strong attacks from the Young Germans and was almost denied a list seat, only avoiding this fate due to threats of resignation from the old-line <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democrats</span>. The conflict between the Young Germans and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">democrats</span> is so intense that not one of the <span style="color: #D3D3A9;">**VNR**</span>'s candidates could be selected without resistance from local organizations. [? if dvp_ideology == "Right": At least the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has shown a strong stance against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, which cannot be said for the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, who remain bitter over the debacle caused by the formation.?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="both">!}[? if flavour_6_trigger and flavour_6_trigger_time == time: The lack of attention Hugenberg's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> has devoted to attacking [? if nsdap_leader == "Hitler": Adolf Hitler?][? if nsdap_leader == "Goebbels": Joseph Goebbels?]'s <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> is looking to be a blunder of enormous proportions. Despite the party's silence dealing with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span>, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> aren't returning the favor, and have a lot to gain from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> attacking us on their behalf. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s goal of rallying the conservative and nationalist forces around themselves is ultimately benefitting the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> more than it is helping themselves. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 9 and dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": [? if dnvp_leader == "Hergt": With the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s party congress just two months away, Hergt and his ruling old guard preside over a relatively stable party. However, two key issues remain contentious: Treviranus and his Young Conservatives advocate for a shift toward democracy, while the question of cooperation with the rising <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> looms large, as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> threaten to eclipse the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> as the dominant force on the right. ?][? if dnvp_leader == "Lambach": Over the past few months, Lambach has made increasing enemies within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> as he pushes his <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Social</span> ideals into the party platform and expands the role of workers and trade unions within the party. Many aligned with the old guard and the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing now threaten to defect to the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> if Lambach continues to sideline their interests. ?][? if dnvp_leader == "Treviranus": Treviranus has increasingly clashed with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s old guard, led by national conservatives like Westarp, over his push to embrace democracy and sideline monarchism as official party policy. Additionally, his positions on key "national questions"—especially on reparations—mark a radical departure from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>’s traditional stance. ?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 9 and dvp_leader == "Scholz" and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : The severe atrophy of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s vote share and party organizations has sparked internal opposition against their party leader Ernst Scholz, who many believe is responsible for derailing negotiations towards bourgeois concentration. Walther Schnell—the leader of one of their district organizations—is fed up with Scholz's inaction and urges him that the very fate of the German bourgeoisie depends on its consolidation into a single party. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if dkp_merger_timer == time + 2 and (dvp_leader == "Dingeldey" or dvp_leader == "Hugo") : Troubled by the surge of far‑right populism and the emboldened left, Germany’s heavy‑industry financiers have begun quietly pressuring the KVP/DNVP and the DVP to discuss tighter cooperation. The industrialist backers hope that the two parties working closer together will help bolster their leverage in the Reichstag. Members in both the KVP/DNVP and DVP, notably Treviranus and Dingeldey, are optimistic about these potential meetings.After weeks of behind the scenes pressure, the KVP/DNVP and the DVP have formally begun a series of joint meetings aimed at coordinating legislative strategy in the Reichstag. While Treviranus and Dingeldey lead the talks with cautious optimism, reservations linger among the KVP/DNVP’s agrarian wing, who fear further influence from the city focused industrial interests in the DVP. The DVP’s moderate wing is similarly resistant, as they see this as another step away from Stresemann’s legacy. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if dkp_merger_timer == time + 1 and (dvp_leader == "Dingeldey" or dvp_leader == "Hugo") : After weeks of careful deliberation, the KVP/DNVP and the DVP have made unexpectedly rapid strides in aligning their party platforms and coordinating candidate selection. That momentum has put a formal merger squarely on the table. Treviranus and Dingeldey applaud the unprecedented unity, openly acknowledging that a full merger could be on the horizon. Both the DVP’s moderate wing and the KVP/DNVP’s agrarians are still voicing concerns, but find their resistance increasingly sidelined as the broader majority coalesces around deeper integration. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if dkp_merger_timer == time + 2 and dvp_leader == "Glatzel" : Seeking to see off the surge of far‑right populism and the emboldened left, the KVP/DNVP and the DVP have begun to discuss tighter cooperation. Their aim is that an alliance could bolster their leverage in the Reichstag and help maintain their support. Members in both the KVP/DNVP and DVP, notably Treviranus and Glatzel, are optimistic about these potential meetings. After weeks of secret meetings, the KVP/DNVP and the DVP have formally begun a series of joint meetings aimed at coordinating legislative strategy in the Reichstag. While Treviranus and Glatzel lead the talks with cautious optimism, reservations linger among the KVP/DNVP’s agrarian wing, who fear further influence from the urban middle class interests in the DVP. The DVP’s moderate wing is similarly resistant, as they see this as another step away from Stresemann’s legacy. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if dkp_merger_timer == time + 2 and dvp_leader == "Glatzel" : After weeks of careful deliberation, the KVP/DNVP and the DVP have made unexpectedly rapid strides in aligning their party platforms and coordinating candidate selection. That momentum has put a formal merger squarely on the table. Treviranus and Glatzel applaud the unprecedented unity, openly acknowledging that a full merger could be on the horizon. Both the DVP’s moderate wing and the KVP/DNVP’s agrarians are still voicing concerns, but find their resistance increasingly sidelined as the broader majority coalesces around deeper integration. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_12_trigger and flavour_12_trigger_time == time: Our decision to tolerate Brüning's government, while appreciated, has become a significant liability that will severely undermine Brüning's support from the more conservative factions of Germany's bourgeois elite. This is especially true among German heavy industry, where they have redoubled efforts to foster a rapprochement between Brüning and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties to prevent the chancellor from becoming overly reliant on our support. Brüning's government's relationship with the capitalist economic interests that initially supported him so enthusiastically has now become increasingly strained. [? if dvp_ideology == "Right" and not lvp_formed and dvp_exist: The right-wing <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> is so displeased by this development that it no longer feels strong loyalty toward Brüning and his government. It’s as if the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> hasn’t already toppled enough governments.?][? if lvp_ideology == "Right" and lvp_formed: The right-wing elements of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> are displeased by this development that it no longer feels strong loyalty toward Brüning and his government. ?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_10_trigger and flavour_10_trigger_time == time : For one reason or another, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> lacks the Reichstag delegates to form a parliamentary faction and is now required to negotiate with another party to join forces. In this case, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has decided to work with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> to establish a parliamentary faction. Surprisingly, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> was interested in accommodating with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" and dstp_formed: but just as they were about to finalize their agreement, an angry Ernst Scholz torpedoed the negotiations, still furious about how the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> disrupted his efforts toward bourgeois unity. Fortunately, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> was able to accept a few defections from the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> to reach the required size for a parliamentary faction.?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz" or not dstp_formed: [? if chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government: having ceased their intrigues against Brüning's government in order to finalize the agreement.?][? if not (chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government): having put aside their grudges to finalize the agreement.?]?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_11_trigger and flavour_11_trigger_time == time : For one reason or another, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> lacks the Reichstag delegates to form a parliamentary faction and is now required to negotiate with another party to join forces. In this case, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has decided to work with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> to establish a parliamentary faction. Surprisingly, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> was interested in accommodating with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" and dstp_formed: but just as they were about to finalize their agreement, an angry Ernst Scholz torpedoed the negotiations, still furious about how the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> disrupted his efforts toward bourgeois unity. As a result of this, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has formed an agreement with the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> instead, having exhausted its choices. ?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz" or not dstp_formed: [? if chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government: having ceased their intrigues against Brüning's government in order to finalize the agreement.?][? if not (chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government): having put aside their grudges to finalize the agreement.?]?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_32_trigger and flavour_32_trigger_time == time : For one reason or another, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> lacks the Reichstag delegates to form a parliamentary faction and is now required to negotiate with another party to join forces. With the bourgeois parties already grouped together, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is forced to negotiate with them. Surprisingly, the bourgeois parties have gotten over their grudges against the party, and are open to cooperation. [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" and dstp_formed: However, just as they were about to finalize their agreement, an angry Ernst Scholz torpedoed the negotiations, still furious about how the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> disrupted his efforts toward bourgeois unity. Fortunately, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> was able to accept a few defections from the various parties within the group to reach the required size for a parliamentary faction.?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz" or not dstp_formed: [? if chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government: They have all agreed to cease their intrigues against Brüning's government in order to finalize the agreement.?][? if not (chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government): With past disputes set aside, they've finalized the agreement.?]?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_33_trigger and flavour_33_trigger_time == time : For one reason or another, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> lacks the Reichstag delegates to form a parliamentary faction and is now required to negotiate with another party to join forces. With the bourgeois parties already grouped together, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is forced to negotiate with them. Surprisingly, the bourgeois parties have gotten over their grudges against the party, and are open to cooperation. [? if dvp_leader == "Scholz" and dstp_formed: However, just as they were about to finalize their agreement, an angry Ernst Scholz torpedoed the negotiations, still furious about how the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> disrupted his efforts toward bourgeois unity. As a result of this, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is forced to enter the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]'s parliamentary group. ?][? if dvp_leader != "Scholz" or not dstp_formed: [? if chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government: They have all agreed to cease their intrigues against Brüning's government in order to finalize the agreement.?][? if not (chancellor == "Brüning" and not spd_in_government): With past disputes set aside, they've finalized the agreement.?]?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_54_trigger and flavour_54_trigger_time == time : The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, for one reason or another, lacks the necessary Reichstag delegates to form a parliamentary faction. As a result, it is forced to conclude an agreement [? if wp_r + ddp_r >= 3.6: with the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> and other minor bourgeois parties?][? if wp_r + ddp_r < 3.6: to enter the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]'s parliamentary group?]. The merger of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> into the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> has effectively ruled out the possibility of a unified liberal parliamentary group. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 9 : In the small Free State of Brunswick, elections are held, resulting in [? if not brunswick_hitler: another majority for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>?][? if brunswick_hitler: a victory for the bourgeois unity list and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, who enter government together despite our plurality of votes?]. [? if brunswick_hitler: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> is expected to use their new position in government to grant Hitler citizenship, as he remains stateless. ?]?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 9 : Adolf Hitler of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> has taken an oath of legality, pledging to use constitutional means to gain power. This occurred during a court case involving <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> members and Reichswehr officers Richard Scheringer and Hanns Ludin, who were accused of plotting a national uprising by establishing <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> cells within the Reichswehr. Under normal circumstances, Hitler's statements—tantamount to preparing for high treason—would have led to prosecution. Instead, the authorities are tolerating, even legitimizing the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> agenda. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_18_trigger and flavour_18_trigger_time == time: The <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, once an enthusiastic supporter of Brüning's bourgeois government—and the only special interest party to secure a cabinet position—is now scrambling to extricate itself from government following its electoral defeat. While the party reports gains from expanding its electoral base into new states, these are more than offset by disproportionately heavy losses in the regions where it first found success. The same trend can also be observed with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>. Currently, a divisive internal struggle has emerged between chairman Hermann Drewitz and the party’s anti-Brüning faction on the right. The latter seeks to compel the resignation of their sole minister from the government, aiming to pressure Brüning into abandoning his reliance on our votes and instead forming a coalition with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_29_trigger and flavour_29_trigger_time == time: The <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>, once an enthusiastic supporter of Brüning's bourgeois government, is now scrambling to distance itself following its electoral defeat. While the party has gained from expanding into new states, these are more than outweighed by steep losses in its original strongholds. A similar trend can be seen with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>. An internal power struggle has emerged between the pro-Brüning faction—led by party chairman Hermann Drewitz and Justice Minister Johann Bredt—and increasingly anti-Brüning district organizations. These anti-Brüning factions are demanding that the party pressure Brüning into forming a coalition with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>[? if spd_toleration:&nbsp;to reduce his dependence on our votes?], or they threaten to dissolve or even break away from the party. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 10 and spd_prussia: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> is once again attempting to destabilize and polarize Germany amidst the economic depression following the failed Young Plan referendum. At their annual congress, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span> announced plans for a referendum to prematurely dissolve the Prussian Landtag. Frustrated by the dominant position the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> have held in Prussia since the founding of the Weimar Republic, they seek to force new elections that would better reflect the national shift to the right. [? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical":Despite strong enthusiasm from other right-wing parties,?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate":This is met with skepticism from the right-wing parties, and?] Hitler himself has shown little interest in the initiative and has refused to commit the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, even as some <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> leaders express strong support. [? if dvp_ideology == "Right" and not in_grand_coalition_prussia and (dvp_leader == "Scholz" or dvp_leader == "Dingeldey"): The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> was also invited to join the "national front," but its leadership has refused to commit as long as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span> remain undecided. The fact that they haven’t outright rejected the offer, is a testament to how far they have strayed from democracy.?] At this stage, the success of the plan appears to hinge on Hitler’s support. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 10 and dvp_leader == "Scholz" and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : Walther Schnell has taken concrete steps in pursuit of his goal of bourgeois concentration, inviting officials from all over Germany to a special conference. The group believes that a parliamentary group of the bourgeois parties isn't enough, and more drastic steps have to be made for the survival of the German middle. Schnell's group aims to take charge in attempting to convince the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s national leadership to support his goals during this month's meeting of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s Executive Committee, which has, unfortunately for them, been delayed until next month. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 10 and dvp_leader != "Scholz" and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : The severe atrophy of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s vote share and party organizations has sparked internal opposition against their party leader [+ dvp_leader +]. Many within the party’s right wing attribute this downturn to its perceived closeness of its leadership with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 10: <span style="color: #009739;">Br</span><span style="color: #FEDD00;">az</span><span style="color: #009739;">il</span> has undergone a revolution, replacing the First Republic with the Second Republic and bringing Getúlio Vargas into power following a disputed presidential election result earlier in the year. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 10 and dnvp_ideology == "Moderate" and (dnvp_leader != "Hergt" or spd_prussia): [? if dnvp_leader == "Hergt": The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span>'s plan to destabilize German democracy by launching a referendum to dissolve the Prussian Landtag has sparked divisions within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. While many in the party support joining the initiative to end <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> control over Prussia, Treviranus and his Young Conservatives oppose it, as it would require cooperation with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>. ?][? if dnvp_leader == "Lambach": Lambach and his supporters have introduced a new party program, notably downplaying monarchism in favor of concrete policies aimed at improving the lives of German workers. This shift has outraged the old guard, who see it as proof that Lambach is advancing the vision he outlined in his "Lambach Article" years ago. With the party congress approaching next month, they are now openly plotting to remove him. At least he has secured Treviranus's support. ?][? if dnvp_leader == "Treviranus": Treviranus and his supporters have introduced a proposal for a renewal of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>'s platform, shifting towards a more <span style="color: #0087DC;">Christian Democratic</span> course. This proposal omits major mentions of monarchism and tacitly supports the current system, albeit with greater presidential powers. This has greatly angered the old guard, [? if not true_christian_democracy: and with their influence over Treviranus, forced him to withdraw the proposal and maintain the status quo.?][? if true_christian_democracy: who believe that monarchism is a core part of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>.?] These differences will have to be resolved in the party congress next month. ?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_58_trigger and flavour_58_trigger_time == time: The National Rural League (RLB) has undergone a significant leadership change due to the growing radicalization caused by the worsening economic and agricultural crisis. This has led to a revolt against the Brüning cabinet's farm policy. As a result, Schiele, the Agricultural Minister and chairman of the RLB, is forced to resign, along with the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>'s Karl Hepp from the RLB's leadership. In their place, Count Eberhard von Kalckreuth, an arch-reactionary and Hugenberg supporter, is elected as the new President. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_57_trigger and flavour_57_trigger_time == time: The Brüning cabinet has introduced the Eastern Aid Act, a policy aimed at relieving the debts of agricultural enterprises in the east—despite the significant financial burden it imposes. This measure directly contradicts Brüning’s broader strategy of economic recovery through budget austerity. To partially fund the policy, the government has retained outdated reparation taxes that became obsolete after the Young Plan. However, the lack of full funding for debt relief has frustrated many influential landowners, prompting them to take their complaints directly to Hindenburg, over whom they wield considerable influence. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 11 and dvp_leader == "Scholz" and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : Schnell's group has successfully elected Eduard Dingeldey to the position of deputy-chairman to Scholz himself. The selection was justified by Scholz's dual role as both chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and head of the Reichstag delegation, and his ongoing health problems. This move was designed to shift the responsibility for revitalizing the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> and implementing Schnell’s plan for a united bourgeois party away from Scholz and toward a more cooperative figure. Due to Scholz's ill health following the appointment of Dingeldey, has ultimately chosen to resign in favor of him. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 11 and dvp_leader != "Scholz" and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : [? if dvp_leader == "Curtius": The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s right wing has successfully established a new deputy chairman position, appointing Eduard Dingeldey with the goal of shifting some of Curtius's responsibilities to him [? if foreign_minister_party == "DVP":due to his preoccupation with his duties as Foreign Minister?][? if foreign_minister_party != "DVP":due to his involvement in governmental affairs?]. However, Curtius has objected to this move, citing Dingeldey's conservative stances—particularly on cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>—and has refused to delegate party leadership to him. This has prompted the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s right wing to begin plotting his removal in next month's Executive Committee meeting.?][? if dvp_leader == "Luther": The broad support Hans Luther enjoyed when he was first elected as leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> last year has eroded, largely due to his stance on constructive cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>. This position has significantly dampened the enthusiasm of the business community, which initially welcomed his leadership. Now, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s right wing is plotting his removal in next month's Executive Committee meeting.?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 11 and dstp_collapsed and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has formally held their party congress to finalize the process of forming the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**State Party**</span>. In an effort for the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to be different from its predecessor, Hermann Dietrich has taken an effort to exclude the pacifists and radical democrats from the new party, to create a more conservative appearance. This has caused the remaining far-left <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**DDP**</span> members to split away, forming the insignificant <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">Radical Democratic Party</span> (<span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**RDP**</span>), only joined by a few Young Democrats. Sadly, good intentions and noble ideas were insufficient in themselves to build a political party. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 11 and dstp_maintained and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer : The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has officially held its party congress to finalize the formation of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**State Party**</span>. The increased number of <span style="color: #D3D3A9;">**VNR**</span> delegates has led the party to adopt a more nationalist platform, using terms like 'national,' 'social,' and '*Volksgemeinschaft*,' while omitting references to '<span style="color: #586593;">democracy</span>' or '<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberalism</span>.' Additionally, the party has worked to exclude pacifists and radical democrats in order to project a more conservative image. This has caused the remaining far-left <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**DDP**</span> members to split away, forming the insignificant <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">Radical Democratic Party</span> (<span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**RDP**</span>), only joined by a few Young Democrats. Sadly, good intentions and noble ideas were insufficient in themselves to build a political party. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 11 : The <span style="color: #C8102E;">Austrian Social Democrats</span> have won the recent legislative election, securing a majority of seats in their <i>Nationalrat</i>. However a right-wing coalition of the <span style="color: #000000;">Christian Social Party</span> and minor bourgeois parties once again has excluded them from government. The Austrian branch of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> have received 3% of the vote, and the political wing of the <span style="color: #ABDDA4;">Heimwehr</span> (comparable to our <i>Freikorps</i>) garnered 6%. This is particularly concerning, as the <span style="color: #C8102E;">Austrian Social Democrats</span> lost votes despite the economic depression occurring while they were in opposition, suggesting the electorate is looking for answers on the right. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_15_trigger and flavour_15_trigger_time == time: The combination of our influence over the Brüning government, the ineffectiveness of his agrarian relief plan, the radicalization of the rural electorate signaled by Martin Schiele's resignation from the RLB, and the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>'s third-place finish in rural areas behind the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span> has led the party to reconsider its support for Brüning. An anti-Brüning right-wing faction now dominates within the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>, successfully pushing through a resolution chastising the Chancellor and demanding a reorganization of the coalition to include the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span>. Brüning has refused to comply, prompting the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> to become one of the first parties to bolt from his coalition, now voting against his decrees and supporting right-wing motions of no confidence. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_25_trigger and flavour_25_trigger_time == time: The general ineffectiveness of Brüning's agrarian relief, led by Agriculture Minister Martin Schiele of the [? if dnvp_split_2: <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?][? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>?], has led to growing dissatisfaction within his own party. To retain their support, Schiele and Brüning have introduced a formal <i>Eastern Aid Act</i>, a policy designed to relieve the debts of agricultural enterprises in the east—despite the heavy financial burden it imposes. While this measure has placated organized agriculture and Hindenburg himself, it stands in direct contradiction to Brüning’s broader strategy of economic recovery through a balanced budget. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1930 and month = 12 and kpd_leader == "Thälmann" : Ernst Thälmann has embraced a new <span style='color: #7A3C00;'>national-populist</span> strategy, rallying under the slogan of the <i>Volksrevolution</i>. This move is an attempt by the <span style='color: #700000;'>**KPD**</span> to expand its influence in the bourgeoisie social groups where the <span style='color: #7A3C00;'>**NSDAP**</span> are the strongest in. Leon Trotsky and many other <span style='color: #700000;'>**Communists**</span> have condemned this shift, denouncing the use of 'people's revolution' instead of 'proletarian revolution' as a distortion of <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span>. They also pointed out that its the exact same slogan used by Otto Strasser and the left-wing faction of the <span style='color: #7A3C00;'>**NSDAP**</span>.  ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_17_trigger and flavour_17_trigger_time == time: The defection of the northern wing’s Reichstag members from the <span style="color: #007A00;">German Peasants' Party</span> to the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> has effectively ended the party as a national political force. All that remains is the original <span style="color: #38C538;">Bavarian Peasants’ League</span>, which, amid a prevailing mood of resignation, is expected to secure only a fraction of its former support in the next election, as most peasants turn further to the right in search of a solution to Germany's crisis. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_19_trigger and flavour_19_trigger_time == time: [? if bruning_time: The <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> has issued a vote of no confidence against Brüning, formally ending any possibility of reconciliation with his government and joining the growing ranks of once-supportive bourgeois parties now in opposition. This decision comes after the party’s sole minister resigned under pressure from its anti-Brüning right wing. He is not alone in stepping down, the party’s?][? if not bruning_time: The <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>'s?] vice chairman and effective propagandist Otto Colosser has also resigned in protest against Drewitz’s "one-man dictatorship," further accusing him of financial impropriety and other shenanigans. The internal strife has escalated to such an extent that numerous local branches have defected, effectively ending the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span> as a viable national political force. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="dnvp">!}[? if flavour_30_trigger and flavour_30_trigger_time == time: Despite pressure from the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>'s anti-Brüning right wing for its lone minister, Johann Bredt, to resign, party chairman Hermann Drewitz has successfully rallied a majority of the parliamentary delegation to support him [? if not in_right_coalition and not in_center_right_coalition: after securing key concessions for the middle class in negotiations with Brüning?][? if in_right_coalition or in_center_right_coalition: after persuading the wider cabinet to abandon tax increases that would have affected the middle class?]. However, this victory comes at a cost—vice chairman and chief propagandist Otto Colosser has resigned in protest, denouncing Drewitz’s 'one-man dictatorship' and accusing him of financial impropriety and other misconduct. The internal strife has escalated to such an extent that numerous local branches have defected, severely weakening the <span style="color: #b8996f;">**WP**</span>'s standing as a viable national political force. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if year = 1931 and month = 1 and dvp_leader == "Dingeldey" and not bourgeois_list and (dnvp_split_2 or kvp_formed) and not lvp_formed and not lvp_merger_2_timer: Despite previous setbacks for liberal and bourgeois unity, the push for closer ties between centrist and moderate right-wing parties remains alive, particularly at the local level. Politicians from the [? if dstp_formed: <span style="color: #E0B0FF;">**Radical Democrats**</span>?][? if not dstp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Democrats**</span>?], the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, and the <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**CSVD**</span> in the State of Hesse have met to discuss closer cooperation. Their initiative has received a surprisingly positive response, leading to the formation of a new national organization and invitations to figures like Hans Luther and Otto Gessler. However, the effort has been disappointing, as many declined to participate[? if spd_prussia:—largely due to the deep divisions caused by the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span>'s planned Prussian referendum, which has split the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> from the rest of the moderate right.?][? if not spd_prussia:—largely due to the strong animosity between the leadership of the national parties.?]?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_23_trigger and flavour_23_trigger_time == time: [+ dvp_leader +] of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has attempted to pressure Brüning into reorganizing his cabinet by removing relatively left-leaning ministers, including their own Julius Curtius, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor Hermann Dietrich, and the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]'s Interior Minister Joseph Wirth. However, these efforts failed to secure majority support within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s Reichstag delegation, forcing [+ dvp_leader +] to put the plan on hold, as he still resents how [+ chancellor +] has effectively excluded his supporting parties in the formulation of his decrees. In the meantime, [+ dvp_leader +] has been working on establishing closer relations with the "<span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>". ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_39_trigger and flavour_39_trigger_time == time: [? if lvp_leader == "Dingeldey": Dingeldey of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> has been scheming to pressure Brüning into removing relatively left-leaning ministers, including their own Vice-Chancellor Hermann Dietrich and the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]'s Interior Minister Joseph Wirth. However, these efforts have sparked strong backlash from nearly all corners of the party. Still, an anti-Brüning right wing is slowly emerging, fueled by resentment over how [+ chancellor +] has effectively excluded his supporting parties from the formulation of his decrees. ?][? if lvp_leader != "Dingeldey": The exclusion of political parties from most of the decision-making in Brüning's government has fueled resentment among those who once enthusiastically supported him, including the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>. Some members of their parliamentary delegation, particularly those from the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, many of whom are also members of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm**</span>, have publicly criticized certain left-leaning ministers, including their own Vice-Chancellor Hermann Dietrich and the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]'s Interior Minister Joseph Wirth. ?] ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_35_trigger and flavour_35_trigger_time == time: [+ dvp_leader +] of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has attempted to pressure Brüning into reorganizing his cabinet by removing relatively left-leaning ministers, including their own Julius Curtius, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor Hermann Dietrich. However, these efforts failed to secure support within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s Reichstag delegation, forcing [+ dvp_leader +] to abandon his plans. The inclusion of the right-wing <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> in the government has led the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>’s right wing to abandon its efforts to court Hugenberg’s <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and Hitler’s <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**NSDAP**</span>, as they believe the cabinet is already sufficiently right-wing. ?]{!</p>!}
{!<p class="other">!}[? if flavour_56_trigger and flavour_56_trigger_time == time: Dingeldey and the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> attempted to pressure Brüning into reorganizing his cabinet by removing relatively left-leaning ministers, including their own Julius Curtius and the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor Hermann Dietrich. However, these efforts failed to gain traction within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>'s Reichstag delegation, and [+ dvp_leader +] strongly condemned the move to oust their own ministers. While the party’s right wing will remain a thorn in Brüning’s side, for now, they are little more than noise. ?]{!</p>!}
